# ~/.config/pj/profiles/scratch -- the throwaway profile `c2` launches (F5a).
#
# Ruled by Gavin at the F5a gate: plugins none, card off, HOOKS ON.
#
# WHY NOT `mode: safe`, which the brief first said. Measured 2026-09-21 from the
# Claude Code docs: --safe-mode disables "CLAUDE.md, skills, plugins, hooks, MCP
# servers, custom commands and agents, output styles, workflows ... and auto memory".
# That is one switch for two very different things. It would drop the start card, which
# is wanted, AND enforce-secret-probe.sh, validate-bash.sh, enforce-uv, enforce-pnpm
# and MemoryRootGuard, which is not: a throwaway worktree would be the least guarded
# session on the machine. `card: off` drops only the card. `mode: safe` stays a
# supported key for P9's baseline measurement; no shipped profile sets it.
#
# THE CONFIG DIR IS FORKED. ~/.claude-scratch is a SIBLING of ~/.claude, never inside
# it (pj-health's sibling row enforces that). Measured: a fresh config dir has no
# credentials and no folder trust, so the FIRST launch on this profile needs a
# `/login` and a trust dialog from a human. pj-health's profile row WARNs while the
# directory is absent, so the owed login is stated rather than discovered.
#
# What forking costs, measured, not assumed: auto memory does NOT travel. A session
# here gets an empty projects/<key>/memory/, so no MEMORY.md is loaded. The drawer,
# the rulings and pj-global are unaffected: open-items and decided always write to
# ~/.claude whatever CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR says.
config_dir:      ~/.claude-scratch
setting_sources: project,local
settings:        ~/.claude/settings.project.json
prompt:          pj-prompt-file
plugins:         none
mode:            normal
card:            off
